  "id": "COMPOUND:42545 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between (4As,10As)-1,1,4A-Trimethyl-7-Propan-2-Yl-2,3,4,9,10,10A-Hexahydrophenanthrene and VMRC-MELG. The compound is directly linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of multiple molecular entities, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one. These latter molecules are both targets of the compound and are themselves linked to VMRC-MELG. This suggests that the compound may act through a series of enzymatic pathways, potentially influencing the activity of VMRC-MELG through the regulation of sialyltransferase activity. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and VMRC-MELG, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
